course: dictionary
lesson: 13950
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word liberated can mean set free, feel free, or taken without asking. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «The soldiers liberated the town» tells you the town was set free from enemy control.
explain: «After the last exam, Mia felt liberated.» Here liberated means free from worry or pressure, because exams are over. Ask yourself: what is the feeling? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some people use liberated as a joke. «Tom liberated the last biscuit from the tin» does not mean he set it free. It means he took it without asking, so the joke is that he borrowed it without permission.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Liberated» means set free from prison, an enemy army or control.
fact: «Liberated» can also mean feeling free from rules, worries or old ideas.
fact: In a joking way, «liberated» means taken or borrowed without asking.
fact: Useful phrases are «liberated from» and «feel liberated».
exercise: «The soldiers liberated the town at the end of the war.» What does liberated mean here? | Painted the town | *Set free from enemy control | Built a new town hall | Took the town's sweets
exercise: Mia says, «I feel liberated now the tests are finished.» What does liberated mean? | Lost and confused | Sure about the answer | *Free from worry and pressure | Tired and hungry
exercise: Tom says, «I liberated a cookie from the jar!» What does liberated mean in this joke? | Opened the jar carefully | Gave it back to Mum | Baked a new cookie for everyone | *Took it without asking
test: «The bird was liberated from its cage in the park.» What does liberated mean in this sentence? | Dropped | Bought | *Set free | Hidden
test: «After the long holiday, Ravi felt liberated from homework.» Which meaning fits best? | Angry | Cold | *Free from a burden | Hungry
exam: Which sentence uses liberated in the joking sense, meaning taken without asking? | The prisoners were liberated at dawn | She felt liberated after the test | The town was liberated after the war | *He liberated the last biscuit from the tin
